    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0184" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v06/pg162"/>

                <head>58. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in the Soviet
                        Union<anchor n="0" xml:id="d58-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-10-06T12:25:00-04:00">October 6, 1962,
                            12:25 p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>826. Following message for delivery soonest to Khrushchev from the President:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Begin Verbatim Text:</hi></p>
                <p>Dear Mr. Chairman:</p>
                <p>I thank you and the Soviet people on behalf of the American people for your
                    congratulations on Commander Schirra’s successful space flight.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d58-f2"/> Your greetings and best wishes have been conveyed to
                    Commander Schirra.</p>
                <p>John F. Kennedy.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">End Verbatim Text.</hi></p>
                <p>Time of release of this message by White House not decided.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Ball</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
